```java
@Transactional
public SlotAllocation allocate(String requestId, String satelliteCode, String stationCode,
        Instant slotStart, Instant slotEnd, Integer expectedVersion) {
    String hash = hash(...);
    // idempotent pre-check
    var existing = allocationRepository.findByRequestId(requestId);
    if (existing.isPresent()) {
        if (existing.get().requestHash().equals(hash)) return existing.get();
        throw conflict(IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT, ...);
    }
    validate slot times
    PassPrediction prediction = predictionRepository.lockLatest(satelliteCode)
        .orElseThrow(notFound);
    if (prediction.superseded()) throw conflict(STALE_PREDICTION) // shouldn't happen since lockLatest returns latest
    if (expectedVersion != null && expectedVersion != prediction.version()) throw conflict(STALE_PREDICTION)
    GroundStation station = stationRepository.findByCode(stationCode).orElseThrow(notFound);
    // lock station row to serialize allocations on the same antenna
    stationRepository.lockById(station.id());
    // checks
    if (slotStart < windowStart || slotEnd > windowEnd) throw WINDOW_GAP
    if (prediction.minElevation < station.minElevation) throw ELEVATION_BELOW_THRESHOLD
    minutes = duration; if minutes*capacity < plannedBytes throw CAPACITY_EXCEEDED
    if (countOverlap > 0) throw ANTENNA_OVERLAP
    insert; catch DuplicateKeyException → re-check idempotent
}
```

Wait: order of checks — 题干 lists "窗口缺口、超容量或同天线重叠". Elevation also. Order doesn't matter much. Note lockLatest FOR UPDATE on latest prediction row serializes with publish (publish does lockLatest then markSuperseded... wait publish locks latest, marks superseded, inserts new. Allocate locks latest (the same row if no new version yet). If publish committed between allocate's lockLatest... no — allocate holds the lock until commit, publish's lockLatest blocks. If publish committed first, allocate's lockLatest returns the NEW latest row (not superseded). So allocate always uses the current latest. expectedVersion check gives STALE_PREDICTION when client specified an old version. Good.

But subtle: allocate locks latest prediction row, publish also locks latest. If allocate starts first (locks v1), publish waits; allocate commits allocation based on v1; then publish proceeds, creates v2, rechecks — allocation not started → rechecked against v2. Correct semantics.

If publish first: allocate locks v2, uses v2. Correct.

Duplicate request race: two concurrent allocates with same requestId → both pass pre-check, both insert → unique constraint violation on one. Catch DuplicateKeyException → findByRequestId → compare hash → return or 409. Need to handle: after DataIntegrityViolation inside @Transactional, the transaction is marked rollback-only in Spring? For JdbcTemplate with DataSourceTransactionManager, catching the exception inside the transaction and continuing — the connection may still be usable (H2 doesn't abort the whole tx on constraint violation, unlike Postgres). Spring only marks rollback-only if the exception propagates through a @Transactional boundary. Catching inside is OK with H2. But safer: pre-check + catch and rethrow as idempotent response. Since H2 allows continuing after constraint violation, fine.

Complete:

```java
@Transactional
public SlotAllocation complete(long id, String requestId, long actualBytes) {
    String hash = hash(id, actualBytes);
    SlotAllocation current = allocationRepository.findById(id).orElseThrow(notFound);
    if (current.status() == COMPLETED) {
        if (current.completionRequestId().equals(requestId)) {
            if (current.completionRequestHash().equals(hash)) return current;
            throw conflict(IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT);
        }
        throw conflict(INVALID_STATE, "已完成");
    }
    if (actualBytes > current.plannedBytes()) throw conflict(ACTUAL_BYTES_EXCEED_PLANNED);
    int updated = allocationRepository.completeIfConfirmed(id, actualBytes, requestId, hash, now);
    if (updated == 0) {
        // lost race with cancel
        throw conflict(INVALID_STATE, "分配已取消或不再可完成");
    }
    return findById(id);
}
```

Also check completion requestId uniqueness globally: if another allocation already used this completionRequestId → 409 IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT. Pre-check findByCompletionRequestId(requestId): if present and its allocation id != id → conflict. Also unique constraint on completion_request_id as backstop.

Cancel:

```java
@Transactional
public SlotAllocation cancel(long id, String reason) {
    SlotAllocation current = findById or notFound;
    if (current.status() == CANCELLED) {
        // idempotent-ish: return current? Spec doesn't require cancel idempotency. If already cancelled with same reason, return current; else 409 INVALID_STATE.
        return current; // keep simple: cancelling cancelled → return current
    }
    if (current.status() == COMPLETED) throw conflict(INVALID_STATE, "已完成，不能取消");
    int updated = cancelIfActive(id, reason, now);
    if (updated == 0) throw conflict(INVALID_STATE, "状态已变化");
    return findById(id);
}
```

